# Q2 Weekly Terminal Status

## Use For

Prepare the standing Monday terminal status brief: berth holds, contractor windows, sailing impacts, and open punch lists across Pier 9, Seaglass, HarborPass, drill weekends, and Pier 7 ramp work.

## Load First

- [[plan-q2-terminal-readiness]] - master checklist for closures, badge counts, notices, and sailings alignment.
- [[juno-castillo]] - who owns the playbook and signs off passenger-facing disruption calls.
- [[p9-gate-retrofit]] - gate delivery slip, critical path, lighting, and Turnstile crew windows.
- [[p9-gang-replacement]] - gangway delivery hold, mock-up width, hose spec, and load-test gates.
- [[sg-refit]] - drydock progress, crane booking, sea trial date, and return-to-service checklist.
- [[marcus-holt]] - berth swaps, Friday Harbor diversions, and back-to-back shift bans on Pier 9.

## Working Context

Walk the six codenames in playbook order; never collapse P9-GATE and P9-GANG into one line.
Gate slipped to May 28; gangway held May 21 — if someone cites a single Pier 9 date, ask which vendor.
Crane ground truth is May 19, not the early Marcus email. HarborPass is done; Pier 7 legacy readers sunset Jun 12.
Flag coverage-matrix drift (3 vs 4 deckhands) only if SSB-DRILL staffing comes up; otherwise leave it for Priya's after-action.
