# Pier 9 Gate Commissioning Brief

## Use For

Brief Victor Dunn, Cal Donner, Fatima Okonkwo, or Marcus Holt before gate commissioning, floodlight cutover, contractor badge deactivation, or the week-8 Q2 closeout on Pier 9.

## Load First

- [[p9-gate-retrofit]] - four fare lanes, Turnstile scope, and gate-specific night lighting — not gangway work.
- [[decision-critical-path-p9-gate]] - why berth closures and Marcus's reordering still treat gate as the driver.
- [[decision-floodlight-maintenance]] - Cal's maintenance-mode cutover on 2026-06-03; gangway lane stays lit.
- [[turnstile-dynamics]] - gate vendor, May 28 delivery slip, and commissioning crew windows.
- [[pier-9]] - shared berth rules: no back-to-back gate and gangway shifts on the same berth.
- [[decision-revenue-return]] - Seaglass revenue return the same week sets the closeout rhythm for all piers.

## Working Context

Lead with codename P9-GATE — if the room says "gangway," "hydraulic hose," or "2.4 m mock-up," you are on P9-GANG.
Night lighting and floodlight maintenance mode are gate-only; do not promise gangway circuit changes.
Confirm Turnstile punch list before badge deactivation; Fatima issued 14 temp badges for the gate crew week.
Kelwick and the single-contractor plan are dead — split vendors under the Q2 playbook are the only active track.
Close with sailing restoration: once gate commissioning clears, Marcus can release the Pier 9 berth holds tied to the critical-path declaration.
